From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Krzysztof Kozlowski <krzysztof.kozlowski@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 14:35:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 005/117] soc: qcom: smp2p: Fix out-of-bounds with incorrect
 DTB of too many outbound entries

The outbound SMEM item has a fixed array of SMP2P_MAX_ENTRY (16)
entries, thus driver should be sure that DTB does not have more of
these, otherwise such incorrect DTB would cause out-of-bounds writes.

Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Closes: https://sashiko.dev/#/bug/linux-eaf9beb4-cc0d-4d8e-be28-4c12b039b3c8
Fixes: 50e99641413e ("soc: qcom: smp2p: Qualcomm Shared Memory Point to Point")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Krzysztof Kozlowski <krzysztof.kozlowski@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261102133531.173434-5-krzysztof.kozlowski@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Bjorn Andersson <andersson@kernel.org>

[mzak: picked for q91o (21 Nov gains plan) from linux-next/maintainer tree commit be72e07d0393; mark V]

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
index 5c53110bc1e05..051ac6c7f0eaf 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
@@ -539,6 +539,11 @@ static int qcom_smp2p_outbound_entry(struct qcom_smp2p *smp2p,
 	struct smp2p_smem_item *out = smp2p->out;
 	char buf[SMP2P_MAX_ENTRY_NAME] = {};
 
+	if (out->valid_entries >= SMP2P_MAX_ENTRY) {
+		dev_err(smp2p->dev, "too many outbound entries\n");
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	/* Allocate an entry from the smem item */
 	strscpy(buf, entry->name, SMP2P_MAX_ENTRY_NAME);
 	memcpy(out->entries[out->valid_entries].name, buf, SMP2P_MAX_ENTRY_NAME);
